      "id": 492832,
      "username": "paulroberts",
      "name": "Paul",
      "created_at": "2026-01-29T09:02:23.208Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hi, thanks for the reply. I thought it was Frappe CRM that was being discontinued and the CRM was being integrated into ERPNext? Anyhow, I tried the option to install from marketplace but this is looking like a separate install - and now it’s asking for a “valid payment mode” - as I’m just trialling this I’m not paying for anything yet. Anyhow, I somehow ended up on the frappe cloud dashboard and found my “site”, then was able to install the CRM module from there. So now I have a pink Frappe CRM icon appearing on my desktop, but I have no idea if this is the built in ERPNext CRM or the separate CRM. I guess I will have to have a play and see what happens.</p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/d/0/d0aebbae7c43552ac198aeaf507708f5af617bf0.png\" data-download-href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/d0aebbae7c43552ac198aeaf507708f5af617bf0\" title=\"image\"><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/d/0/d0aebbae7c43552ac198aeaf507708f5af617bf0_2_690x244.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"tM5G1H7kQlV9rcZgr7C76IpVuG4\" width=\"690\" height=\"244\" srcset=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/d/0/d0aebbae7c43552ac198aeaf507708f5af617bf0_2_690x244.png, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/d/0/d0aebbae7c43552ac198aeaf507708f5af617bf0_2_1035x366.png 1.5x, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/d/0/d0aebbae7c43552ac198aeaf507708f5af617bf0.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"EBF2FC\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">1258×445 25.8 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>",
